  "decision": "SysML 8.2.2.6.3 states DefaultReferenceUsage : ReferenceUsage = RefPrefix Usage. Deviation DefaultReferenceUsage (follow_xtext) makes two changes, both the SysML Xtext's: an optional bare 'end', and a declaration that is not empty. By the clause's letter RefPrefix, UsageDeclaration (through a nullable Identification) and ValuePart can all be empty and UsageBody can be ';', so a lone ';' is a member. The Xtext's UsageDeclaration requires a name or a FeatureSpecializationPart. The rule writes Usage out as its declaration and UsageCompletion so the declaration can be required: a name, short and/or long, optionally specialized, or a FeatureSpecializationPart alone, as Identification (KerML 8.2.3.1) and UsageDeclaration (SysML 8.2.2.6.2) state them.",
